  "key_findings": [
    "1. LEVEL-3 NEGATIVE (registered): none of the four constructions reproduces Im S = i pi c/6 in an exact lattice evaluation. Combined with SIM-2026-076 (the literal object has exactly real pseudo entropy by chiral symmetry; the paper's regulator restores the real part but not the imaginary part), the imaginary part of timelike entanglement entropy is, on the critical TFIM lattice, a property of the continuum analytic continuation and not of any lattice transition matrix examined here.",
    "2. Breaking the chiral symmetry does produce imaginary parts, but they are not the CFT phase: at zero regulator they are branch counts (tens); with the regulator they are small and non-monotonic in the field, returning to the symmetric residual as h_z -> 0. One size-and-setting point lands within 10 percent of pi/12; the same setting at the other sizes does not.",
    "3. The c = 1 Dirac control does not rescue the imaginary part: same behaviour as c = 1/2, identity gate exact.",
    "4. Continuous branch tracking from real temperature does not recover pi c/6 either: at zero regulator the tracked phase is a large multiple of 2 pi (mode wrapping through trace zeros), and with the regulator it is small.",
    "5. Method: exact pseudo-entropy on the lattice is branch-convention dependent whenever tau_A's eigenvalues wrap; any lattice statement about Im S must specify the convention, and three conventions (per-eigenvalue principal, per-mode principal, tracked) disagree by O(1) or more where wrapping occurs."
  ],
  "claim_level": "Level 3 negative within the registered scope (four constructions, sizes as run). Not a theorem about all lattice constructions. No novelty claim without the section-8 gate; finding 1 may be known in the pseudo-entropy literature and a search is owed before any wording stronger than 'we did not find'.",
  "counterfactual_novelty": "Registered outcome space YES/NO per candidate; all NO occurred. The single-size C1 point and the h_z non-monotonicity were not anticipated.",
  "what_would_change_this": "A registered construction outside these four that produces a stable pi c/6 (e.g. an MPS pseudo-entropy at h_z = 0.02 over L = 32..128 showing the C1 trend saturating at pi/12 rather than peaking), or a demonstration that the continuum phase is convention-fixed by a physical requirement the lattice evaluations violated.",
  "downstream_actions_required": [
    "HYP-2026-032.json: status -> LEVEL-3 NEGATIVE (registered), with the C1 trend flagged as the only candidate for a registered follow-up.",
    "Story chapter 13.",
    "PLAN-2026-09-06.md HYP-032 section: DONE with this outcome; next decision is Jon's (follow the C1 thread with an MPS method, or close)."
  ],
